---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import pageMeta from "@/data/page-meta.json";

const meta = pageMeta["/docs/recipes"];
---

<Layout title={meta.title} description={meta.description}>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow">Recipes</p>
    <h1>Compositions, not registry items</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">
      Recipes show how the registry components fit together. They are documentation
      only: <code>loseta add</code> never installs a recipe, and the markup uses the
      same public classes and state contract as the component pages.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-grid">
      <a class="docs-card" href="/docs/recipes/form">
        <span class="docs-card-title">Form</span>
        <span class="docs-card-description">Field layout, native validation, choices and actions.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="docs-card" href="/docs/recipes/data-table">
        <span class="docs-card-title">Data table</span>
        <span class="docs-card-description">A table with selection, status badges and row actions.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="docs-card" href="/docs/recipes/date-picker">
        <span class="docs-card-title">Date picker</span>
        <span class="docs-card-description">A calendar composed with a popover and a trigger.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="docs-card" href="/docs/guidelines/typography">
        <span class="docs-card-title">Typography</span>
        <span class="docs-card-description">The type scale, prose defaults and the reading rules.</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2>Why recipes are not items</h2>
    <p>
      A registry item has a stable root selector, a documented anatomy and one style
      file per declared style. A recipe has consumer data, column definitions or a
      date library; shipping it as CSS would either hard-code a data model or ship
      behavior. Recipes stay in the docs so the registry can remain CSS-only.
    </p>

    <h2>Remaining shadcn names</h2>
    <p>
      Two shadcn names are not visual components and do not become registry items:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Direction</strong> is the native <code>dir</code> attribute and logical
        properties. See <a href="/docs/theming#direction">Direction</a> in Theming.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sonner</strong> is a toast library. The <a href="/docs/components/toast">Toast</a>
        component documents it as a compatibility note; add the library in consumer code.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Typography is a guidelines page because the registry already styles prose through
      the base layer. There is no separate <code>typography</code> class to install.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
